course: dictionary
lesson: 13461
title: Words that show shame
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a moment feels inside. Humiliating means making you feel very ashamed and foolish in front of other people. «Her spelling test was humiliating, because she wrote her name wrong on the board and everyone laughed.» The clues are «in front of everyone» and «laughed», so the feeling is shame, not just a small moment of embarrassment.
explain: Humiliate is the verb: it means to make someone feel very ashamed. Humiliating is its -ing form, so you can say «a humiliating experience» or «humiliating someone in public». Check the verb by putting it into a sentence: if the word fits after «The bully tried to», it is probably humiliate.
explain: To find the feeling, ask yourself: who saw it, and what did they do? If people were laughing or pointing, the word is probably humiliating. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Humiliating means making you feel very ashamed and foolish in front of other people.
fact: Humiliate is the verb; humiliating is also its -ing form, as in «humiliating someone in public».
fact: «A humiliating defeat» means a loss that makes you feel ashamed, not just a loss.
fact: Sharing humiliating photos or messages of other people online is bullying, and you must report it to a trusted adult.
exercise: «Falling over in the playground while everyone laughed was humiliating.» What does humiliating mean here? | Making you feel very sleepy | *Making you feel very ashamed and foolish | Making you feel very cold | Making you feel very proud
exercise: «He lost the race by ten metres, a humiliating defeat.» What kind of defeat is this? | *A shameful, embarrassing one | A close and exciting one | A wet and muddy one | A quiet, peaceful one
exercise: Find and copy the verb form of humiliating. | humid | humour | *humiliate | hum
test: «Someone shared a humiliating message about a classmate online.» What should you do? | Laugh at it and save it | Ignore it and do nothing at all | *Report it to a trusted adult | Share it with more friends
test: Which word is closest in meaning to humiliating? | Pleasing | *Shameful | Lucky | Quiet
exam: What does «humiliate» mean? | *Make someone feel very ashamed and foolish | Make someone feel very tired | Make someone feel very hungry | Make someone feel very proud
